1
00:05:28,571 --> 00:05:34,571
Sabotage of Hitler's ingenious weapons of mass
destruction...the V1 and V2 rockets!

2
00:10:57,142 --> 00:11:03,142
Operation Crossbow is a drama, war, thriller film directed by Michael Anderson.

3
00:16:25,714 --> 00:16:31,714
Allied agents infiltrate the Nazi rocket complex at Peenemunde in
order to obtain their secrets and sabotage the plant.

4
00:21:54,285 --> 00:22:00,285
The film alternates between German developments of the V-1 missile and V-2 rocket (with a German
cast speaking their own language) and discovery by British Intelligence of the weapon.

5
00:27:22,857 --> 00:27:28,857
Nora Van Ostamgen, played by Sophia Loren.

6
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:57,428
Lt. John Curtis, played by George Peppard.

7
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Professor Lindemann, played by Trevor Howard.

8
00:43:48,571 --> 00:43:54,571
General Boyd, played by John Mills.

9
00:49:17,142 --> 00:49:23,142
Duncan Sandys, played by Richard Johnson.

10
00:54:45,714 --> 00:54:51,714
Robert Henshaw, played by Tom Courtenay.

11
01:00:14,285 --> 01:00:20,285
Operation Crossbow (later re-released as The Great Spy Mission) is a 1965
British espionage thriller set during the Second World War.

12
01:05:42,857 --> 01:05:48,857
This film is loosely based on an actual series of events where British undercover operatives
targeted the German manufacturing facilities for experimental rocket-bombs.

13
01:11:11,428 --> 01:11:17,428
The film was directed by Michael Anderson and stars Sophia Loren, George Peppard,
Trevor Howard, John Mills, Richard Johnson, and Tom Courtenay.

14
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
The screenplay was written by Emeric Pressburger (under the pseudonym "Richard Imrie"), in collaboration
with Derry Quinn and Ray Rigby, from a story by Duilio Coletti and Vittoriano Petrilli.

15
01:22:08,571 --> 01:22:14,571
It was filmed in Panavision and Metrocolor at MGM-British Studios.

16
01:27:37,142 --> 01:27:43,142
Although it is largely fictional, the movie does touch on the main aspects of the operation, which was
geared to thwart the German long-range weapons programme in the final years of World War II.

17
01:33:05,714 --> 01:33:11,714
The story alternates between Nazi Germany's development of the V-1 flying bomb and V-2 rocket,
and the efforts of British Intelligence and its agents to counter those threats.

18
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
All characters speak in the appropriate language, with English
subtitles for those speaking German or Dutch.

19
01:44:02,857 --> 01:44:08,857
The film explores themes of nazi, rocket, metrocolor.

20
01:49:31,428 --> 01:49:37,428
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
